## Multiple Readers, Exclusive Writer

`RwLock[T]` (Read-Write Lock) allows many readers OR one writer, similar to XIOM's borrow rules but enforced at runtime across threads.

### Read and Write Locks

```xiom
let lock = RwLock.new(42);

// Read lock — multiple allowed
let r1 = lock.read();
let r2 = lock.read();  // OK — multiple readers
let v1 = *r1;  // 42
let v2 = *r2;  // 42

// Write lock — exclusive
// let w = lock.write();  // would block while readers exist
```

### RwLock vs Mutex

| Feature | Mutex | RwLock |
|---------|-------|--------|
| Readers | 1 (exclusive) | Many (shared) |
| Writers | 1 (exclusive) | 1 (exclusive) |
| Use case | Always exclusive | Read-heavy workloads |
| Cost | Lower | Higher |

### When to Use RwLock

```xiom
// Read-heavy cache
let cache = Arc.new(RwLock.new(Map[Int, Str]()));

// Many threads can read simultaneously:
fn lookup(cache: &RwLock[Map[Int, Str]], key: Int) -> Option[Str] {
  let map = cache.read();  // shared read — doesn't block other readers
  return map.get(&key);
}

// Writers are exclusive:
fn update(cache: &RwLock[Map[Int, Str]], key: Int, value: Str) -> Unit {
  let mut map = cache.write();  // exclusive write — blocks all others
  map.insert(key, value);
}
```

### Preventing Writer Starvation

RwLock may prioritize writers to prevent starvation:

```xiom
// If readers keep coming, writer might wait forever
// Implementation may queue writers ahead of new readers
```

